                <pb facs="0741" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-12T16:00:00-04:00">June 12, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Your 135, May 24, 6 p.m. The Department concurs in the view expressed in
                    paragraph 2 of your telegram. You are authorized to proceed in the manner and
                    under the conditions set forth in the Department’s 64, April 22, 2 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
